The source hands me the whole exploit chain. Lets break down what it reveals, 

The allow-list check (this is the key):

python
ALLOWED_HOSTS = {"kestrel.thm"}
host = (urlparse(target).hostname or "").lower()
if host not in ALLOWED_HOSTS: abort(403)

It only forwards requests where the hostname is exactly kestrel.thm. And the comment tells me the trick: 
“Internal hostname resolves to 127.0.0.1 via /etc/hosts on this box.” So on the target, kestrel.thm → 127.0.0.1. 
That means a URL like http://kestrel.thm/admin/notes passes the allow-list and hits localhost.

